  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 0757563d).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe creation-time family refusal (`family_gate` in `crates/app/src/commands/operation/gates.rs`) said \"the setup's machine is a mill\" when no machine was mounted. An unmounted setup reads as a mill by default (the kind_of law), so the words misstated it. Verdict unchanged; only the clause differs:\n\n- no machine mounted: `... the setup has no machine mounted - mount a lathe (or a mill-turn) first` (turning), `... the setup has no machine mounted - mount a plasma table first` (plasma)\n- machine mounted: unchanged, e.g. `... the setup's machine is a mill - mount a lathe (or a mill-turn) first`\n\nThe \"milling work ... is a lathe\" sibling has no no-machine case (an unmounted setup is judged as a mill, so milling ops are never refused there), so it is untouched.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `the_family_door_names_both_sides` (turning.rs): asserts the no-machine wording and that \"is a mill\" is absent.\n- `a_mounted_mill_refusal_names_the_mill` (turning.rs, new): pins the mill wording when a mill is mounted.\n- `the_plasma_family_lives_on_a_plasma_table_only` (plasma_profile.rs): pins the plasma no-machine wording.\n\nQuick gate green on the final head (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nNot exercised: the full batch/release tiers.\n\n## Merge order\n\nOpen PR #1290 (#1215, the lathe/mill post cell table) also pins these creation-time messages. Whichever merges second may need the old text replaced by the no-machine wording where it applies.\n\nNot changed: the palette tooltip in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs` still says \"The document's machine is a mill\" for an unmounted document. It is a tooltip, not the creation-time refusal, so it is left for a follow-up issue.\n\nChangelog: A refusal on a setup with no machine mounted now says so (\"the setup has no machine mounted\") instead of naming a mill. (#1291, PR pending)\n\nFixes #1291\n",
